# What Vercel does not need to build the demo surface.
#
# The web app is `app/` plus `data/proof-artifact.json`. The Foundry project, the proving
# pipeline's build output and every local test artifact are irrelevant to the deployed page and
# only slow the upload down. Nothing here is required at runtime: `/api/proof` reads the chain
# over plain JSON-RPC and needs no key, no wallet and no `.env`.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and must stay that way.
# These are gitignore semantics: a bare `lib/` matches a directory named `lib` at ANY depth, not
# just this repo's Foundry `lib/`. That silently excluded `node_modules/next/dist/lib/**` from the
# deploy upload, and `vercel deploy --prebuilt` then failed on the runner with
#   ENOENT: lstat '/vercel/path0/node_modules/next/dist/lib/constants.js'
# because `.vc-config.json` lists those files in its `filePathMap` (1506 of its 1570 entries point
# into node_modules) and expects the deploy step to ship them. `out/` and `cache/` are the same
# trap — npm packages contain directories with both names.

/lib/
/out/
/cache/
/broadcast/
/.next/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/.lighthouseci/
/docs/index41-pitch-deck.pdf
